    "notes": "Doxorubicin cardiotoxicity is mediated by TOP2B (off-target isoform) in post-mitotic cardiomyocytes, distinct from its anti-tumor activity via TOP2A. Dexrazoxane is the only FDA-approved cardioprotectant (Phase 4), acting by TOP2B degradation. The NRF2/KEAP1 and ROS detoxification pathways provide endogenous cytoprotection. SGLT2 inhibitors and ARBs are being tested as emerging cardioprotective strategies in 7 clinical trials."
